WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.500
From inside the dark bar, the camera looks through a diamond-latticed window at wet Lower East Side storefronts and a backwards neon OPEN sign.

00:05.500 --> 00:10.500
The camera glides along the back bar: rows of bottles, an old register, and fluorescent sections that stop on either side of it.

00:10.500 --> 00:14.500
A low view passes a foamy pint, condensation on the glass, and a rocks cocktail resting on its coaster.

00:14.500 --> 00:19.000
The view crosses the room and lowers past the three-shade fixture toward green cloth, a cue ball, and fifteen tightly racked balls.

00:19.000 --> 00:23.000
The cue strikes. Balls scatter across the table as the camera drifts down the east side; the 7 ball and then the 4 ball fall into the southeast corner pocket.

00:23.000 --> 00:26.800
From low along the east rail, the camera follows the 13 ball, the last ball still moving, until it stops.

00:26.800 --> 00:30.000
The camera rises and pulls back to reveal the settled table, booths, bar, overhead fixture, and lit storefront at the far end of the room.
